A||||13||batboy||Do the dew (strips)||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||03-08-2000||07:41 AM||||A couple of my Fieros need the dew strips, you know, those outer door window rubber seals that fall apart after 15 years of service. Is there a cheaper source for them other than the Fiero Store? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||03-08-2000||09:36 AM||||Try the dealer. Strangely enough, I've seen them cheaper, there. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||03-08-2000||10:09 AM||||Try this link to an old thread in the Technical Forum:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000442.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000442.html</A> <P>I found this AFTER I had ordered from the FieroStore so I never called to see if the price/availability is the same.<P>If you've not done this before, ya might want to go and at least look at the tool Rodney Dickman sells to see what you will need -- before you start (unlike me!). I found this link AFTER I ran across the two inaccessible screws.  Showed the photo of the tool to a neighbor and he welded me one in a few minutes....<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-08-2000||12:10 PM||||Raydar, the local Pontiac dealer wanted about the same price as the Fiero Store for the dew wipes. Thanks mbramble! After I checked out that old Forum topic, I called Kevin Burdette at Chriswell Chevrolet (888-466-9101) and ordered two pairs of those outer window seals for a total cost of $22.13 each. Is this Forum great or what? You guys just saved me over $60! I have another order ready to place with Rodney Dickman, which includes that little dew strip tool he makes. Thanks!<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||2M4 Dale||03-08-2000||12:35 PM||||Go to <A HREF="http://www.lustineparts.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lustineparts.com/</A>   I got mine there. I think about $21.00.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mbramble||03-08-2000||12:43 PM||||I really wish that I had found that information before I ordered from the FieroStore!!!  Oh well, live and learn....||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||03-08-2000||07:18 PM||||what are the GM part numbers for those. (both sides) Mine are both shot. the drivers one is almost all gone. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gokart||03-08-2000||07:31 PM||||I second that mbramble! Paid $84.00 for both sides!||||reg||4
Z||000008||mbramble||03-08-2000||08:52 PM||||Ogre,<P>The link to the old thread I mention above (http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000442.html) has the part numbers you need.<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||cobra427||03-08-2000||10:35 PM||||all,here are the part#'s for both inner and outter "Sealing Strips" <P>Outer:R/H...20606220--L/H 20606221<BR>Inner:R/H...20320534--L/H 20320535<P>These are considered type2 84-88<BR>There is a type1 for 84's that have a different part #<p>[This message has been edited by cobra427 (edited 03-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||DJRice||03-09-2000||10:43 AM||||I just did that job several weeks back.  Got the parts from Criswell Chevrolet (kevin burdette) for $45 including shipping.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||03-09-2000||07:14 PM||||I've looked at the 84 door since someone mentioned awhile back that the strips are diferant....... looks like the later ones should fit, but they will look diferant. You might need to drill a hole or 2 for the new outer ones, I had no way to check that.<P>The dif is that the original ones have a bit of a flap that covers the top edge of the outer door skin.||||reg||1
Z||000012||cobra427||03-09-2000||09:23 PM||||Ogre,<BR>The part #'s for the 84's are:<BR>R/H...20320532<BR>L/H...20320533 (both are outter S/Strips)<BR>The difference between the type 1&2 are as follows;type 1 uses push-in retainer for attachment. <BR>        type 2 uses hang-on retainer for attachment.<p>[This message has been edited by cobra427 (edited 03-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Spyder||03-09-2000||09:36 PM||||I replaced mine on the 84 and they fit in, no problem. I didn't notice the difference.||||reg||1
